
  Arch Linux Kairo install medium

  1. Connect to the internet (iwctl for Wi-Fi).
  2. Run archinstall. Choose your disk, bootloader, and a sudo-enabled user.
     Select the Hyprland desktop profile and NetworkManager for a desktop install.
  3. Reboot into the installed system, log in as that user, and run kairo-setup.

  Kairo is bundled at /opt/kairo; package installation needs internet access.
  Archinstall asks you to review disk changes before installation.
  Documentation: /opt/kairo/iso/README.md

